e of <italic>Mycobacterium tuberculosis</italic> in regions of Southern Africa.</article-title><source>Int J Tuberc Lung Dis</source> <year>2007</year>;<volume>11</volume>:<fpage>311</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17352098</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R20"><label>20. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Lopez</surname> <given-names>B</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Aguilar</surname> <given-names>D</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Orozco</surname> <given-names>H</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Burger</surname> <given-names>M</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Espitia</surname> <given-names>C</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Ritacco</surname> <given-names>V</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>A marked difference in pathogenesis and immune response induced by different <italic>Mycobacterium tuberculosis</italic> genotypes.</article-title><source>Clin Exp Immunol</source> <year>2003</year>;<volume>133</volume>:<fpage>30</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2249.2003.02171.x</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12823275</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R21"><label>21. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Dormans</surname> <given-names>J</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Burger</surname> <given-names>M</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Aguilar</surname> <given-names>D</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Hernandez-Pando</surname> <given-names>R</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Kremer</surname> <given-names>K</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Roholl</surname> <given-names>P</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>Correlation of virulence, lung pathology, bacterial load and delayed type hypersensitivity responses after infection with different <italic>Mycoba